* ============================================================
* LANGUAGE SHAKEDOWN CANARY
* Messaging-normalization lane -- runtime proof that the
* es / fr / de / it locale rows resolve for every command
* localized in the messaging pass.
*
* Status: RUNTIME_PROVEN / REVIEWED 2026-07-16
* Safety: REPORT_ONLY / SMOKE
* Purpose: prove compiled locale selection, localized command USAGE rendering,
*   and the INDEXSEEK result-payload boundary after corrective audit.
* Inputs: current built runtime and compiled/active message catalog.
* Outputs: reviewed launcher-console transcript named by the invoking proof command.
* Mutation: session locale only; reset to en-US; no DBF, index, LMDB, HELP, or files.
* Fixture: none; command USAGE surfaces plus a no-table INDEXSEEK result probe.
* Gate: maintainer-authorized corrective proof; reject unexplained errors or fallback.
*
* NON-DESTRUCTIVE:
*   - USAGE forms only. Opens no table, mutates no data or files.
*   - Safe to run with SET ERRORSTOP OFF.
*
* WHAT IT PROVES:
*   - SET LANGUAGE <loc> switches the active message locale
*     (cli::Settings::message_locale).
*   - Each localized command's USAGE block renders in that locale
*     via cli::cmdout::print_message -> format_message(id,vars,locale),
*     i.e. it exercises the compiled es/fr/de/it locale table, not
*     just the en-US fallback.
*   - Catalog-level coverage via SET MESSAGE CATALOG CHECK and
*     SET LANGUAGE REPORT <locale>.
*   - INDEXSEEK result output remains a stable machine-facing payload and is
*     not routed through the localizable message catalog.
*
* HOW TO READ IT:
*   - Under each locale banner, every USAGE block should print with
*     the localized labels:
*       en-US : Usage:/Examples:/Notes:
*       es    : Uso:/Ejemplos:/Notas:
*       fr    : Utilisation :/Exemples :/Remarques :
*       de    : Verwendung:/Beispiele:/Hinweise:
*       it    : Uso:/Esempi:/Note:
*   - Command keywords, placeholders and paths stay in English by design.
*   - If a block prints English labels under a non-en locale, that
*     command's locale row failed to resolve.
* ============================================================
SET ECHO ON

* ------------------------------------------------------------
* 00. Catalog integrity (concise validation signal)
*   SET LANGUAGE REPORT <locale> is available for a full per-symbol
*   coverage dump, but is intentionally omitted here to keep this
*   regression entry lean. Use it interactively when auditing gaps.
* ------------------------------------------------------------
ECHO === LANGUAGE SHAKEDOWN CANARY ===
SET MESSAGE CATALOG CHECK
SET LANGUAGE CHECK

* ------------------------------------------------------------
* 01. BASELINE -- en-US (expect Usage:/Examples:/Notes:)
* ------------------------------------------------------------
SET LANGUAGE en-US
ECHO --- en-US : localized command USAGE sweep ---
ROLLBACK USAGE
DELETE USAGE
RECALL USAGE
ERASE USAGE
IMPORT USAGE
EXPORT USAGE
CREATE USAGE
ZAP USAGE
PACK USAGE
COPY USAGE
COMMIT USAGE
TURBOPACK USAGE
REBUILD USAGE
SORT USAGE
REINDEX USAGE
SCX USAGE
EXPORTFUNCTIONS USAGE
INDEXSEEK USAGE

* ------------------------------------------------------------
* 02. SPANISH -- es (expect Uso:/Ejemplos:/Notas:)
* ------------------------------------------------------------
SET LANGUAGE es
ECHO --- es : localized command USAGE sweep ---
ROLLBACK USAGE
DELETE USAGE
RECALL USAGE
ERASE USAGE
IMPORT USAGE
EXPORT USAGE
CREATE USAGE
ZAP USAGE
PACK USAGE
COPY USAGE
COMMIT USAGE
TURBOPACK USAGE
REBUILD USAGE
SORT USAGE
REINDEX USAGE
SCX USAGE
EXPORTFUNCTIONS USAGE
INDEXSEEK USAGE

